          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Does that need treating?",
          "answer": "I can't tell you whether 6.4 needs treatment. The guidance I can access does not give a treatment threshold for total cholesterol, and I can't fill that gap from general knowledge.\n\nThe \"Lipids: screening intervals, risk stratification and statin initiation\" guidance (major cardiology society consensus guidance) says the treatment decision depends mainly on your estimated 10-year risk of heart and blood vessel disease, not on one cholesterol number. It also says a non-fasting sample is acceptable for initial screening in most adults. The passages did not say how to calculate that risk or what level calls for treatment.\n\nAsk a clinician:\n- Whether my 10-year cardiovascular risk should be calculated, using my age, blood pressure, smoking status, diabetes status and family history.\n- Whether I need my LDL, HDL and triglyceride results to make the decision.\n- Whether a treatment decision is needed now or whether retesting makes more sense.\n\nDo not start, stop or change any medication based on this number alone.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
