          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "What would the alternative be first?",
          "answer": "The guidance I can access does not say what the first-line alternative to treatment is for a high cholesterol result. The search returned no passage on lifestyle or other first-line options for cholesterol.\n\nThe search did return two passages from other topics, and they don't apply here:\n\n- The hypertension guidance (blood pressure) describes lifestyle measures first for some cases. That is about blood pressure, not cholesterol, so I can't carry it over.\n- The type 2 diabetes and anxiety guidance cover different conditions.\n\nThe lipid guidance (\"Lipids: screening intervals, risk stratification and statin initiation\") says treatment is driven mainly by estimated 10-year cardiovascular risk. It does not describe what to do first for people below a treatment threshold.\n\nAsk a clinician:\n- Whether lifestyle changes are a suitable first step for me, and what they would involve.\n- What my 10-year cardiovascular risk is, and what that means for whether treatment is needed.\n- Whether retesting is more useful than acting on one result.\n\nDo not start, stop or change any medication based on this number alone.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
